-  <p class="rodd-why"><b>RoDD is the metric this catalog is priced on.</b> Net profit divided by the worst
-  peak-to-valley drawdown: this system&rsquo;s window (8 months) returned
-  <b>1,505%</b> on its drawdown. Shown at Multiplier 5; one multiple draws down
-  <b>$1,600</b> at worst (best window).</p>
-  <p class="ro-lead">This amount is your DRAWDOWN BUDGET, not your account size.</p>
-  <p class="ro-warn">We recommend the drawdown never exceeds 25% of your account balance (a $2,500 drawdown budget means a $10,000 account or more). Raising the Multiplier raises profit and drawdown together and is inherently risky.</p>
